        <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">At the Minchah and Maariv services, the Chazzan recites the Whole Kaddish on page 000. The congregation says עָלֵינוּ on page 000, and mourners recite Kaddish on page 000.</tei:note>
        <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">On the first two nights of Pesach, some congregations recite הַלֵל on page 000, and then continue as above. On the second night of Pesach, the Counting of the Omer, page 000, is said, and then continue עָלֵינוּ as above.</tei:note>
        <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">On Sukkos, לְדָוִד ה' , page 000, is said after עָלֵינוּ .</tei:note>
        <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">On Friday night, וַיְכֻלוּ , page 000 is recited before the Chazzan<tei:hi rend="italic"> recites the Whole Kaddish.</tei:hi></tei:note>
        <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">At Shacharis, הַלֵל , page 000, is said. The Chazzan then recites the Whole Kaddish, and the service continues with the Order of the Reading of the Torah on page 000.</tei:note>
